but first the latest on our top story  the goodwill of the Olympic Games  appears to be thawing relations between  North and South Korea not the North's  leader Kim jong-un invited South Korea's  president to Pyongyang for a summit in  hopes of easing tensions between the  rival nations the message was delivered  by Kim's sister today just hours after  the Winter Games opened in South Korea  she travelled to the south as part of  the North's delegation to the Olympics  Ben Tracy is in the Olympic city of  Pyeongchang  Ben good morning good morning South  Korean president moon jae-in has said  that he wants these to be the peace  Olympics and a turning point for  relations here on the Korean Peninsula  and it looks like he may be getting his  wish  president moon hosted Kim jong-un's  sister kim yo-jong today at the blue  house in seoul during that meeting she  told moon that Kim Jong moon wants him  to visit the North Korean capital at the  earliest date possible for what would be  the third inter-korean summit since the  Korean War now at the opening ceremony  of the Winter Olympics Friday night here  in Pyeongchang moon and Kim shook hands  in what was deemed a historic moment US  vice president Mike Pence was sitting in  a row in front of her but the two never  spoke during the ceremony athletes from  North and South Korea marched together  under a unified flag symbolizing their  hope for a more peaceful future now  president moon has not officially  accepted this invitation to go to North  Korea but he apparently told Kim Jong  Un's sister they should create the  conditions that would make that possible  in the future this could complicate the  Trump administration's plan of using  sanctions to try to isolate North Korea  and convince it to give up its nuclear  weapons program  Alex Ben Tracy at the Winter Olympics in  South Korea thanks Ben
 

